# SYNOPSIS

```usage
guide
```

# DESCRIPTION

guide shows the manual in a window, as AmigaGuide showed its documents: a row of buttons, Contents, Index, Retrace, and Browse's ◀ and ▶, over the place the viewer is at.

When it starts it reads every page under `/lib/man` once, and opens at the Contents: each section, and each page in it with its summary.
The Index is every page's name, its other names and its keys, in order, each with the page it leads to.
A page is shown as man(1) prints it, and every `name(N)` in it, N from 1 to 8, is a link to that page.
A link, a page in the Contents and a word in the Index only move the viewer to a page of the manual: nothing a page names is ever run.
Retrace goes back to the place before, as far back as the viewer has been.
Browse goes to the page before or after this one in its section.

guide listens on the plumber's `man` port: the plumber's rule sends any text that is `name(N)` there, so a page named in a terminal, a document or a window opens in guide (plumber(4)); with guide not running, the plumber refuses it.
It is an app (manifest(6)'s `app Guide`), listed in Deskbar's menu.

# FILES

: `/svc/guide/status`
  Read only, a line each: where the viewer is, `place contents`, `place index` or `page <name>(<n>)`; `history <n>`, the places Retrace can go back to; `pages <n>`, the pages read; and `port man` once it listens on the plumber's port, else `no port`.
: `/svc/guide/ctl`
  Write only, a command a write: `go <name>(<n>)`, `contents`, `index`, `retrace`, `next` and `previous`, as the buttons and links do.
: `/lib/man`
  The pages.

